6.2 Security Requirements

The CAP platform security requirements are derived from military simulation data protection needs, enterprise security standards, and cloud-native security best practices. These requirements ensure the platform maintains appropriate security controls for handling sensitive distributed simulation data across multiple environments.

Functional Security Requirements

Authentication Requirements

REQ-AUTH-001: Multi-Factor Authentication
- The platform MUST implement enterprise-grade authentication using Firebase JWT tokens
- Authentication tokens MUST include automatic key rotation capabilities
- Token validation MUST occur at the API Gateway edge before reaching backend services
- Authentication MUST support both direct Firebase token validation and Kong Gateway header forwarding

REQ-AUTH-002: Session Management
- User sessions MUST be stateless using JWT tokens with configurable expiration
- Session tokens MUST include user identity, email, and consumer ID claims
- Token refresh MUST be handled transparently without user intervention
- Session invalidation MUST be supported for security incidents

REQ-AUTH-003: Service Authentication
- Internal service-to-service communication MUST use secure authentication mechanisms
- Health check endpoints MAY remain publicly accessible for monitoring purposes
- Administrative endpoints MUST require elevated authentication privileges
- API Gateway MUST validate all incoming requests before routing to backend services

Authorization Requirements

REQ-AUTHZ-001: Role-Based Access Control
- The platform MUST implement fine-grained role-based access control (RBAC)
- User roles MUST be enforced at both API Gateway and application levels
- Service accounts MUST follow principle of least privilege
- Authorization decisions MUST be logged for audit purposes

REQ-AUTHZ-002: Endpoint Protection
- Data manipulation endpoints MUST require authenticated user access
- Public endpoints (health, authentication) MAY allow unauthenticated access
- Administrative endpoints MUST require elevated privileges
- API rate limiting MUST be enforced per user and per endpoint

REQ-AUTHZ-003: Resource Access Control
- Database access MUST be restricted to authorized services only
- File system access MUST be controlled through Kubernetes security contexts
- Network access MUST be governed by network policies and firewall rules
- Container registry access MUST use encrypted credentials

Data Protection Requirements

REQ-DATA-001: Encryption in Transit
- All external communications MUST use HTTPS/TLS encryption
- Internal service communications SHOULD use mTLS where feasible
- Database connections MUST use encrypted channels
- Message queue communications MUST be encrypted

REQ-DATA-002: Encryption at Rest
- Persistent data MUST be encrypted using cloud provider encryption services
- Kubernetes secrets MUST be encrypted at rest
- Container images MUST be stored in encrypted registries
- Log files containing sensitive data MUST be encrypted

REQ-DATA-003: Data Classification and Handling
- Simulation data MUST be classified according to sensitivity levels
- Personal identifiable information (PII) MUST be handled according to privacy regulations
- Data retention policies MUST be implemented and enforced
- Data disposal MUST follow secure deletion procedures

Network Security Requirements

REQ-NET-001: Network Segmentation
- Production, staging, and development environments MUST be network-isolated
- Kubernetes namespaces MUST implement network policies for micro-segmentation
- External traffic MUST be filtered through API Gateway
- Internal traffic MUST be controlled through service mesh or network policies

REQ-NET-002: Traffic Management
- API Gateway MUST implement rate limiting to prevent abuse
- DDoS protection MUST be enabled at cloud provider level
- Traffic monitoring and anomaly detection MUST be implemented
- Load balancing MUST distribute traffic securely across service instances

REQ-NET-003: Firewall and Access Control
- Cloud provider firewalls MUST restrict access to necessary ports only
- Kubernetes ingress MUST be configured with appropriate access controls
- Administrative access MUST be restricted to authorized IP ranges
- VPN or bastion host access MUST be required for administrative operations

Compliance and Governance Requirements

REQ-COMP-001: Audit and Logging
- All authentication and authorization events MUST be logged
- Security events MUST be forwarded to centralized logging system
- Audit logs MUST be tamper-evident and retained according to policy
- Log access MUST be restricted to authorized personnel only

REQ-COMP-002: Vulnerability Management
- Container images MUST be scanned for vulnerabilities before deployment
- Runtime vulnerability scanning MUST be implemented for deployed containers
- Security patches MUST be applied within defined timeframes
- Vulnerability assessment reports MUST be generated regularly

REQ-COMP-003: Incident Response
- Security incident response procedures MUST be documented and tested
- Automated alerting MUST be configured for security events
- Incident escalation procedures MUST be defined and communicated
- Post-incident analysis and remediation MUST be conducted

Operational Security Requirements

REQ-OPS-001: Secrets Management
- Application secrets MUST be stored in Kubernetes secrets or external secret management
- Secrets MUST be encrypted at rest and in transit
- Secret rotation MUST be automated where possible
- Secret access MUST be logged and monitored

REQ-OPS-002: Container Security
- Container images MUST be built from trusted base images
- Containers MUST run with non-root users where possible
- Container capabilities MUST be restricted to minimum required
- Container runtime security MUST be monitored

REQ-OPS-003: CI/CD Security
- Build pipelines MUST include security scanning and testing
- Deployment pipelines MUST validate security configurations
- Code repositories MUST implement branch protection and review requirements
- Deployment artifacts MUST be signed and verified

Environment-Specific Requirements

Development Environment Requirements
- Authentication MAY be simplified for developer productivity
- Security scanning SHOULD be performed but MAY not block deployments
- Network access controls MAY be relaxed for debugging purposes
- Logging verbosity MAY be increased for troubleshooting

Staging Environment Requirements
- Security configurations MUST mirror production environment
- DAST security scanning MUST be performed on all deployments
- Performance testing MUST include security load testing
- Security validation MUST be completed before production promotion

Production Environment Requirements
- All security controls MUST be fully implemented and enforced
- High availability MUST be maintained for security services
- Security monitoring MUST provide real-time alerting
- Change management MUST include security impact assessment

Monitoring and Alerting Requirements

REQ-MON-001: Security Monitoring
- Real-time monitoring MUST be implemented for authentication failures
- API Gateway metrics MUST include security-related events
- Database access patterns MUST be monitored for anomalies
- Network traffic MUST be analyzed for suspicious activity

REQ-MON-002: Performance Monitoring
- Security controls MUST NOT significantly impact system performance
- Authentication latency MUST be monitored and optimized
- Rate limiting effectiveness MUST be measured and tuned
- Security scanning performance MUST be optimized for CI/CD pipelines

REQ-MON-003: Compliance Monitoring
- Security policy compliance MUST be continuously monitored
- Configuration drift MUST be detected and remediated
- Security control effectiveness MUST be measured and reported
- Compliance reporting MUST be automated where possible

Testing and Validation Requirements

REQ-TEST-001: Security Testing
- Unit tests MUST include security-focused test cases
- Integration tests MUST validate authentication and authorization flows
- End-to-end tests MUST include security scenario testing
- Performance tests MUST validate security controls under load

REQ-TEST-002: Penetration Testing
- Regular penetration testing MUST be conducted by qualified professionals
- Automated security scanning MUST be integrated into CI/CD pipelines
- Vulnerability assessments MUST be performed quarterly
- Security testing results MUST be tracked and remediated

REQ-TEST-003: Disaster Recovery Testing
- Security controls MUST be validated during disaster recovery testing
- Backup and restore procedures MUST include security considerations
- Business continuity plans MUST address security incident scenarios
- Recovery time objectives MUST account for security validation requirements

These security requirements provide a comprehensive framework for implementing, maintaining, and validating the security posture of the CAP platform across all environments and operational scenarios.